        "---\n",
        "## 2. Define the Metrics and the Baseline\n",
        "**Goal:** decide how models will be judged and set a bar every model has to beat."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6hk-NfyWen-J"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Write-up note (metrics and method):**\n",
        "I judge every model with three regression metrics:\n",
        "- **R-squared (R2):** the share of the variation in income rank that the model explains. 1 is perfect, 0 is no better than guessing the average, and a negative value is worse than guessing the average.\n",
        "- **MAE (mean absolute error):** the average size of a miss, in income-rank units. An MAE of 0.03 means predictions are off by about 3 percentile points of income rank on average. This is the easiest metric to explain.\n",
        "- **RMSE (root mean squared error):** like MAE but it punishes big misses more, so it shows whether a model makes occasional large mistakes.\n",
        "\n",
        "To compare models fairly I use **cross-validation on the training set only**: the training data is split into 5 parts, and each part takes a turn as a mini test set while the model trains on the other 4. Models that need tuning (ridge, lasso, random forest) tune themselves inside each training fold (nested cross-validation), so the score is not flattered by tuning on the same data. The real test set stays untouched until the end."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "j6PE09WFen-J",
        "outputId": "5d2edd64-e5cb-449d-87c0-bed5cc8c1116"
      },
      "execution_count": 4,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Baseline (average)   CV R2 = -0.029 (+/- 0.010 SE) | MAE = 0.0713 | RMSE = 0.0845\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Cross-validation setup and a helper that scores any model (nested CV for models that tune themselves)\n",
        "outer_cv = KFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n",
        "inner_cv = KFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=7)\n",
        "\n",
        "scoring = {\"r2\": \"r2\",\n",
        "           \"mae\": \"neg_mean_absolute_error\",\n",
        "           \"rmse\": \"neg_root_mean_squared_error\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "cv_results = {}   # name -> dict of per-fold scores\n",
        "\n",
        "def cross_validate_model(name, model):\n",
        "    scores = cross_validate(model, X_train, y_train, cv=outer_cv, scoring=scoring)\n",
        "    cv_results[name] = {\"r2\": scores[\"test_r2\"],\n",
        "                        \"mae\": -scores[\"test_mae\"],\n",
        "                        \"rmse\": -scores[\"test_rmse\"]}\n",
        "    r2 = cv_results[name][\"r2\"]\n",
        "    print(f\"{name:20s} CV R2 = {r2.mean():.3f} (+/- {r2.std(ddof=1) / np.sqrt(len(r2)):.3f} SE) | \"\n",
        "          f\"MAE = {cv_results[name]['mae'].mean():.4f} | RMSE = {cv_results[name]['rmse'].mean():.4f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Baseline: always predict the training average\n",
        "baseline = DummyRegressor(strategy=\"mean\")\n",
        "cross_validate_model(\"Baseline (average)\", baseline)"
      ]
    },
