      "source": [
        "**Write-up note (when to use ridge and lasso):**\n",
        "Ridge and Lasso are linear regression with a penalty on large coefficients, which helps when predictors overlap (like the income, education, and race-share columns in my data). **Ridge** shrinks all coefficients toward zero and keeps every predictor. **Lasso** can shrink some coefficients all the way to zero, which acts as automatic feature selection. The strength of the penalty (`alpha`) is a hyperparameter, so I tune it with cross-validation (`RidgeCV` and `LassoCV` do this internally). I use these when I expect a linear relationship but want more stable coefficients than plain linear regression gives."
      ]
